 resource (like a buffer).</li><li data-ref="58ce523c-0206-49c9-a1c1-df9084d0d8d3"><strong data-ref="47023e24-df5c-4a15-a098-b2235a740970">Consumer</strong>: This thread takes data (items) from the shared resource for processing or consumption.</li></ul><p data-ref="a2d286d1-9e47-4488-89f3-63403f95ccf7" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="697f60a2-6b45-402f-bea7-e220772c5a0e"></p><p data-ref="29585c08-9b8e-402c-a040-8b32c5765261" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">The problem revolves around coordinating these threads such that:</p><ul data-ref="5ffd3b57-3159-451b-82d0-615fc8850a24" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="3c12f533-ccc4-44d4-876c-a2d127670b77">The producer does not produce when the buffer is full.</li><li data-ref="1ce3fc22-0391-40b0-ab61-af425afeaecf">The consumer does not consume when the buffer is empty.</li><li data-ref="2d3f68d8-69b5-4adb-953b-f3286f1c18d7">Both threads operate safely without corrupting the shared resource.</li></ul><p data-ref="8142fcc0-9ab7-47b2-b5e8-55ccff65c7e3" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="06f24105-2094-4ac2-b59a-1bc93e576b5d"></p><p data-ref="4e0d3b70-2c85-48c0-adb3-15eeefd45b46" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">To achieve synchronization in Java, we can use the synchronized keyword along with wait and notify methods to control the interaction between the threads.</p><p data-ref="345c220d-b13d-419c-bcfd-ceb6317e8f06" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="644367b8-68a5-477b-8ee3-ad68f95929c2"></p><p data-ref="4e69e4e5-70a0-414a-aaed-9b2af673a55c" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><strong data-ref="b6ee6d36-d94d-4aea-8180-6b9fe296b4d6">Input Format:</strong></p><ul data-ref="6dc248fb-15e9-41b9-9a7b-de9fa50eea8d" data-counter-list-1-reset="0"