d black;" data-ref="460032e2-bed1-4533-aa9b-d38c003943c3" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="45cbbf09-1bb6-42b9-9c00-ca44b28edea5"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="6364b8a9-c583-4864-a8f4-86f30fac01a3"><p data-ref="b05e2712-3924-46ed-9f33-dc28c8646fb7" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Write a Java program using synchronized threads, which demonstrates producer consumerconcept.</p><p data-ref="367cf2ae-54e4-4e18-b547-74a509fcfab9" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="1cd8622d-fb85-4152-90e0-3789952e6f5e"></p><p data-ref="f7e7a94c-824b-4709-b924-cac0669c5f27" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">The Producer-Consumer problem is a classic synchronization problem in computer science. It involves two types of threads:</p><ul data-ref="31e6f8f0-acf4-46b4-956b-a52972d04c88" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="aa6c42d7-449b-4de4-bab4-dfef87a20818"><strong data-ref="9d0d0df2-0b23-4911-9080-a2c0856fba6d">Producer</strong>: This thread generates data (e.g., items) and places it in a shared resource (like a buffer).</li><li data-ref="58ce523c-0206-49c9-a1c1-df9084d0d8d3"><strong data-ref="47023e24-df5c-4a15-a098-b2235a740970">Consumer</strong>: This thread takes data (items) from the shared resource for processing or consumption.</li></ul><p data-ref="a2d286d1-9e47-4488-89f3-63403f95ccf7" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="697f60a2-6b45-402f-bea7-e220772c5a0e"></p><p data-ref="29585c08-9b8e-402c-a040-8b32c5765261" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">The problem revolves around coordinating these threads such that:</p><ul data-ref="5ffd3b57-3159-451b-82d0-615fc8850a24" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="3c12f533-ccc4-44d4-876c-a2d127670b77">The producer does not produce when the buffer is full.</li><li data-ref="1ce3fc22-0391-40b0-ab61-af425afeaecf">The consumer does not consume when the buffer is empty.</li><li data-ref="2d3f68d8-69b5-4adb-953b-f3286f1c18d7">Both threads operate safely without corrupting the shared resource.</li></ul><p data-ref="8142fcc0-9ab7-47b2-b5e8-55ccff65c7e3" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="06f24105-2094-4ac2-b59a-1bc93e576b5d"></p><p data-ref="4e0d3b70-2c85-48c0-adb3-15eeefd45b46" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">To achieve synchronization in Java, we can use the synchronized keyword along with wait and notify methods to control the interaction between the threads.</p><p data-ref="345c220d-b13d-419c-bcfd-ceb6317e8f06" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="644367b8-68a5-477b-8ee3-ad68f95929c2"></p><p data-ref="4e69e4e5-70a0-414a-aaed-9b2af673a55c" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-lis