ata-ref="0614e11e-19d0-4e54-92a6-08ab08741930" data-undisplayed="undisplayed">Aim:</b><br data-ref="f3d01778-5c6a-49a3-9aae-0073f2a1f986"><span class="question-text ql-editor" data-ref="63f9f024-ee19-42eb-bd3e-597de2a3edf3"><p data-ref="4793ec22-6791-4518-94e8-fc8b0ebf5189" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">Create a Java program that demonstrates the use of user and daemon threads. Implement a class <strong data-ref="0d71cb91-215f-4abc-863e-ef53ec0f2c4f">WorkerThread</strong> that extends <strong data-ref="0b589986-9a79-44a8-9a35-0cea2885f70c">Thread</strong> and overrides the <strong data-ref="d6323c30-44d0-4a2b-979b-7069cd2a8740">run</strong> method to simulate some work by printing messages and sleeping for a short duration.</p><p data-ref="ce53320f-64c4-461e-9f99-c980c5fdf80d" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><br data-ref="a660452d-e9e0-49ea-acd1-29945f1537dc"></p><p data-ref="b5e7903b-cca2-47d2-bfd2-fb41c23e2cf1" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">In the <strong data-ref="1272da79-40c9-4e59-9631-40bc534decf1">DaemonThread</strong> class:</p><p data-ref="69f70cac-3e50-4204-bd62-5f16b303f681" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">1. Prompt the user to input the number of user threads and daemon threads.</p><p data-ref="40bcd67f-3f30-48c2-a7d0-fa40b5b717ff" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0">2. Create and start the specified number of user threads and daemon threads.</p><ul data-ref="9ced7b41-9b20-4b40-9969-c078802cfeab" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-counter-list-3-reset="0" data-counter-list-4-reset="0" data-counter-list-5-reset="0" data-counter-list-6-reset="0" data-counter-list-7-reset="0" data-counter-list-8-reset="0" data-counter-list-9-reset="0"><li data-ref="79135f80-a14d-4e2a-8ddf-c225b25b4c56"><strong data-ref="31ec17ee-d5bc-41cd-85ce-e0496ba92dbe">User Threads: </strong>These threads will run to completion and are not interrupted by the main thread.<strong data-ref="19381ba0-cf5d-4c7a-a9bd-38ea0c091e86">Daemon Threads:</strong> These threads will run in the background and may be terminated abruptly when the main thread exits.</li></ul><p data-ref="90b011b4-fc2b-4d9e-85c0-72be10fb9a04" data-counter-list-1-reset="0" data-counter-reset="list-1 list-2 list-3 list-4 list-5 list-6 list-7 list-8 list-9" data-counter-list-2-reset="0" data-cou